ENTRY            20299   20251214   20260826   20260826       2323
SUBENT        20299001   20251214   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                 11         24
TITLE      Angular distributions of fragments in fission of
            uranium and thorium induced by 14 MeV neutrons
AUTHOR     (A.Katase)
INSTITUTE  (2JPNKYU)
REFERENCE  (J,MEK,21,81,1961)
FACILITY   (CCW,2JPNKYU) 500 kV Cockcroft-Walton accelerator
INC-SOURCE (D-T) 170 keV deuteron on TiT
SAMPLE     Two samples were prepared for (1) loaded emulsion
            method and (2) plate camera method.
           Results obtained by these methods are not appreciably
            different, and the weighted average of these results
            was adopted.
DETECTOR   (TRD) Loaded emulsion method and plate camera method
            were applied
           (SCIN) Plastic scintillator (0.2 mm in thickness and
            1.6 cm in diameter) for associated alpha detection
METHOD     (ASSOP) Total number of neutrons obtained by counting
            associated alpha particles
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No information on sources of uncertainty
HISTORY    (19711010C)
           (19740626E)
           (19840106E)
           (20071218A) DATA-ERR changed to ERR-S. Data corrected.
           (20251214A) ON. Recompiled. 004-007 added.
ENDBIB              24
